  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empower Southern Africa activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Zimbabwe):  Agriculture is the backbone of rural development in Zimbabwe and consists of such processes as irrigation, production, processing, packaging, transportation and storage of agricultural produce. The electrification of these agricultural processes is crucial to ensure agriculture is more economically productive, efficient, sustainable, and climate proofed. However, electricity supply from the national grid is hampered by inefficiencies and inadequate hydropower generation of electricity that makes up about 50 percent of Zimbabwe&apos;s energy supply. Therefore, this activity will facilitate the electrification of these processes through increased access to renewable energy. It will coordinate with USAID activities in three provinces to provide technical assistance and support to:.i. Conduct technical surveys, market assessments, and in-depth analysis of the potential, challenges, and opportunities for Productive Use of Renewable Energy (PURE) in the selected provinces; and .ii. Design or select the best application of PURE to address any identified gaps in the selected provinces..Verifiable performance indicators, outputs and outcomes of this intervention will include:.Number of PURE companies assisted and trained per year per province..Number of PURE equipment deployed per year per province..Number of farmers reached per year per province. .</narrative>
  </description>
